### Definition building

Beyond the initial Trio / Discovery meetings, holding several meetings with Engineering teams to build out descriptions of objectives, key results, user stories, and granular use cases, is all part of definition building.

In addition, this involves creating a PR-FAQ in many cases, or an alternative description of a product feature as an addendum to an existing product (e.g. a new integration). The PR-FAQ should be a prediction of the final product / feature and acts as the root document for a product.

## Development & Delivery

Product Development activities often overlap with Engineering activities. The key difference is the objective to measure the difficult thing that is *impact* of development activity, and quality and efficiency of delivery.

Included in this scope is the delivery concern around team management (in conjunction with Engineering Leads and Managers). This means PMs or DMs (whichever is designated in a team to own the activities) will hold planning, refinement, status, demo, and retrospective meetings around outputs and processes being followed by the team. These inputs usually lead to localised adaptions of the product development process - and therefore it should be viewed as guardrails within which various *agile* systems can be adapted and put into action.

